scp-173 it's a peculiar statue with a  bad attitude and a penchant for  strangulation and snapping necks though  only if nobody has maintained unbroken  eye contact with it some know it as the  sculpture some know it as the peanut  some know it as probably the most  important anomaly of all considering  it's the one that got this whole crazy  affair started but today we're here to  ask an important question do any of us  really know it at all after all its  original file is hardly comprehensive  you might even venture to say it's one  of the most enigmatic scps out there  despite its popularity but today we're  taking a dive beneath the concrete rebar  and krylon brand spray paint to give you  the real inside scoop on scp-173  we've broken into the scp foundation  archive and found 10 different important  files on this infamous vertebrae vandal  and we're going to explore each and  every one of them with you today as you  can expect from the weird and wild scp  foundation they cover possible pasts  presents and futures and some of them  will naturally contradict but that just  gives you more of an opportunity to  immerse yourself and compare them we  often like to believe that the real  truth is somewhere in between so make  sure you pay attention to every detail  throughout so let's get the show on the  road and explore our 10 documents of  interest for scp-173  in hopes of finally getting the complete  story and of course don't blink document  1 crunch where better to start than the  mind of the sinister sculpture itself  crunch gives us an insight into the  private thoughts of this otherwise  pretty uncommunicative monster and  reveals a great deal about its  relationship with its favorite activity  snapping the necks of anyone who dares  to look away from it in crunch scp-173  speaks in very basic broken  rorschach-esque english saying things  like rule dark  people gone  can move  i  happy  trapped for years  kept by a man for research  left alone in room  left to scratch at walls  left to rot and die unless needed  specimen for research prep by self  never seen by others  never spoken  listen  but never speak  see  but never seen  made of rock when others come  free when they not look  prisoner when they look back  i  hate  scp-173 hates and resents its captors  for keeping it confined in its own mind  crunch how it refers to the snapping of  its victim's neck is the only thing that  gives its life a sense of meaning it  will continue to crunch for as long as  it's contained because thanks to the scp  foundation crunch is all it has left  these days document 2 how 173 got to  site 19. this semi-origin story is one  that the fans of this channel will be  familiar with while it doesn't give us  any insight into why this nasty pile of  concrete actually exists it does inform  us why it's currently our problem  scp-173 isn't actually an anomaly native  to our universe however its native  dimension was destroyed by the beast  trapped in scp-2317  the devourer of worlds as is standard  procedure for a universe about to  experience an xk class end of the world  scenario the foundation's department of  extra-dimensional affairs swooped in and  collected all the valuable anomalies  before the world went down the tube one  of these was of course scp-173  which was vacated to site-19 in our  dimension in 1993.  do you think we would have been better  off if we just left him for the devourer  of worlds to take care of let us know  what you think about that down in the  comments document 3 the black moon  sometimes you can be your own worst  enemy if the file on scp-001 the black  moon is to be believed the scp  foundation may actually be behind the  creation of this ornery objed though in  the foundation's defense it was in  service of potentially fighting off a  far more deadly foe the ominous  extra-dimensional being known only as  the black moon one attempt to stop the  black moon from destroying the universe  was known as the key project which  involved creating a number of items  linked to the black moon via conceptual  engineering that would hopefully nullify  its effects the objects needed the  following qualities an inability to act  while under observation a hostility  towards human life and the capacity to  end conscious life if given the  opportunity those three descriptions fit  scp-173 to a t and it was considered the  project's greatest success however it  sadly wasn't enough to actually stop the  horrific rampage of the black moon the  researcher managing the case dr moto was  so ashamed by the failure that he  willingly entered scp-173's containment  chamber and got his neck snapped in the  process  document 4 conclusions regarding  d173263 incident this document finds its  origins in the video analysis of a  foundation researcher with an incredibly  powerful name dr delano smasher dr  smasher had closely observed video  footage of scp-173 killing several  members of d-class personnel and began  formulating a new theory about how 173  actually killed its victims dr smasher  theorized after all that something with  arms as short as scp-173 and no  opposable digits would have trouble  effectively strangling or snapping human  necks according to dr smasher's  observations  scp-173 doesn't actually make any  physical contact with its victims  instead the victims feel oddly compelled  to look at the creature if ever nothing  is looking at it their eyes will snap  open and their heads will twist at any  angle they need to in order to look at  the creature in the eyes it's the sheer  force of this sudden change that often  leads to snapping necks and bruised  faces for the victims not the sculpture  itself physically causing the damage if  dr smasher is to be believed the  sculpture is deadly purely because it  simply demands to be looked at by  somebody at all times document 5  anniversary this brings us nicely to our  next document anniversary positing a  different theory for the mysterious  creation of scp-173  this comes from the perspective of said  possible creator an anomalous entity  that we'll call the artist much like the  unfortunate dr moto the artist an  intelligent being that can seemingly  become invisible and intangible at will  considered  scp-173 to be its finest creation it  viewed scp-173 as a perfect  representation of humanity it does  nothing but bleed and defecate and if  anyone refuses to pay attention to it it  kills them it was a perfect symbol of  the artist's contempt for humanity it  even easily snuck into site 19 to visit  scp-173 on the anniversary of its  creation and found the foundation's lack  of appreciation for this fine creation  as an act of revenge for keeping his  creation locked up and out of sight for  so long he gave the sculpture permission  just once to kill someone who looked  away even if others were still looking  at it for scp-173 this would be  considered a wonderful little treat  document 6 her masterpiece this next  document known as her masterpiece  suggests that scp-173 was created by a  very different kind of artist while this  potential creator of scp-173 was somehow  able to produce an anomaly she was not  anomalous herself just motivated by rage  and revenge she'd been pregnant in the  past but lost the baby due to the  actions of a man whom she considered her  greatest enemy she vowed to make art  from his demise the woman murdered her  enemy with a baseball bat before using  concrete and rebar to build scp-173  around him almost as a way to mock her  fallen foe however like something out of  a horror movie this act of murderous  creation somehow imbued  scp-173 with life when this spiteful  artist had eventually finished the  creation and started to walk away it  claimed her as its first victim the last  thing she remembered hearing was the  sound of concrete scraping against the  ground and then a nasty crunch before  everything went dark document 7  regarding the statue from one tragedy to  another the document regarding the  statue shows the journey of researcher  marcus silburn from idealistic young  employee to full-on mental breakdown  after trying and failing to gain control  of scp-173  he entered the scp-173 project with  bright eyes and big ideas about how to  contain the sculpture suggesting that  the human element be removed entirely in  order to reduce risk to foundation  personnel he proposed ideas like  introducing a sprinkler and drainage  system to the chamber and using a  sentient ai and remote viewing  technology to keep scp-173 immobilized  however he was then enlightened to some  frustrating and frightening facts about  scp-173  in the absence of actual present human  observation the same buildup of feces  and blood that the creature somehow  excretes builds up in any technology  used to control or contain it it  destroys the circuit boards of ais takes  flying camera drones out of the sky and  even degrades the locks on its chambered  doors leading to the brutal death of a  janitor in the hall researcher silburn  advanced far enough through the ranks of  the foundation to be in direct  communication with dr jack bright the  director of site 19. after his final  attempt at containing the creature  without direct human observation  resulted in a containment breach and the  death of 12 people zilburn was moved off  the scp-173 case after breaking down and  begging for permission to terminate the  anomaly permission was denied dr bright  closed the document with a note to a  member of the o5 council reading it can  be surmised that our conclusion was  correct the object for whatever reason  desires or requires human attention and  will not be denied it document 8 a  chance at freedom we once again returned  to the direct perspective of scp-173  but this differs vastly from the  perspective of scp-173's inner monologue  presented in crunch according to the  document entitled a chance at freedom  scp-173 was actually an incredibly  intelligent agent of espionage sent from  another dimension along with its unknown  cadet though the cadet is heavily  implied to be scp-096  this piece details a containment breach  from scp-173's perspective as it is  shown looking down on humanity and its  primitive technology it laments the fact  that it lost its weapon during the  interdimensional transfer and it seethes  that if it still had its weapon this all  would have played out very differently  despite conceding the fact that it  underestimated the humans which was the  main reason it ended up in containment  it spends the majority of the document  touting its own superiority until one of  the scp-131 the ibots turned up and  froze it in place the degree to which  scp-173 hates the ibots cannot be  overstated document 9 experiences with  scp-682  of course no full story video on scp-173  would be complete without a discussion  of the scp-680 cross tests a number of  researchers though particularly the very  persistent dr carlson decided to use  scp-173 in various manners in hopes of  finally doing in that damn lizard in  their first engagement 682 seemed  rightfully frightened of 173 and when a  sniper shot its eyes out 173 immediately  snapped its neck of course it grew back  a series of sniper proof eyes not long  after someone next suggested scp-173  being sent in with a picture of 096  taped to its chest though this was  rejected as being ridiculous and  incredibly dangerous idea to everyone  thank you dr bryant the researchers then  went after scp-682 with high precision  blades cutting it to pieces each of  which became autonomously dangerous  enemies  scp-173 then began to murder each of  those blobs of the mutated tissue until  it stopped when a d-class was sent in to  stare at it while the rest of 682  regenerated  scp-173 was transported back to its cell  but there was a brief power outage  during transit leading 173 to kill a  number of the staff transporting it this  test was still considered a step in the  right direction after 682 was once again  shrunk by a different anomaly  scp-173 was released into its chamber at  first it appeared that 173 had actually  killed 682 but a week later it returned  having reconstituted itself from matter  that had been splattered on 173 after it  had been brutalized making this test  once again a failure dr carlson  requested the resources to conduct one  more cross test but this request was  denied a member of the o5 council  affixed a request simply saying  stop it carlson please  stop it carlson get some help stop it  carlson document 10 revised entry oh  right the time scp-173 literally caused  an xk class end of the world scenario in  the document revised entry we get a  frightening glimpse into a possible  future world where scp-173 develops a  terrifying new anomalous ability  multiplication we don't know exactly how  it happened but here the sculpture  somehow developed the ability to make  exact copies of itself and what's more  every time one of these copies is  produced the collective scp-173 hive  mind gets stronger allowing them to  think tactically and slowly wipe out  north america even destroying any  potential foundation countermeasures  then ripping and snapping through anyone  or anything that dared opposed in the  end the world decided to take the  nuclear option literally and blow away  north america with nuclear bombardment  in order to stop the scp-173 army from  spreading to the rest of the world and  killing everyone however this attempt  didn't actually work as scp-173s were  spotted in wales over in the uk leading  to a second nuclear bombardment it  continued like this until there were no  human beings left to push the big red  button anymore and only the endless  legions of  scp-173 remained there is one bright  side to this otherwise pretty bleak  situation though a group of around 150  scp-173s ganged up on scp-682 and tore  it to shreds somewhere out there dr  carlson is probably smiling now go check  out scp-173 origin story how 173 got to  site-19 and the ipods  scp-131 for more tales involving the scp  foundation's most psychopathic statue
 

